      <p class="research-summary">
        Worked with <a href="https://profiles.sydney.edu.au/jean.yang" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Prof. Jean Yang</a> and
        <a href="https://profiles.sydney.edu.au/clara.grazian" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Prof. Clara Grazian</a> on computational
        method development and benchmarking for spatial transcriptomics.
      </p>
      <ul class="research-bullets">
        <li>
          <span class="research-label">Data preprocessing:</span> Used Python and R to preprocess spatial transcriptomics datasets, including quality
          control, normalization, feature selection, and dimensionality reduction using principal component analysis (PCA).
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="research-label">Spatial domain detection:</span> Applied and compared clustering approaches, including K-means and Seurat,
          alongside spatially informed methods such as BayesSpace and STitch3D, to identify tissue domains and characterize spatial organization.
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="research-label">Method evaluation:</span> Benchmarked clustering performance across simulated and real datasets, examining
          factors affecting method efficacy and identifying strengths and limitations to inform method selection in spatial transcriptomics research.
